{
  "_about": "Signal Box prototype sounds. Pending: genny is not installed in the build container, so this spec waits here until someone renders it with python tools/render_sounds.py signal-box after moving it up to sound-specs/. Each call has its own earcon, and the five are kept apart by kind as well as by place: the points are a heavy iron clank, mono so the game pans them, with points right a tone higher than points left; the signal arm is a ratchet, rising for up and falling for down; ring back is a two-stroke block bell. The tick is a dry, quiet woodblock under the speech. A passing train is a stereo rush with a rail clatter, left to right. Derailing is a long brake screech ending in a heavy crash. The streak chime is a bright rising celesta run. The box ambience is night wind with a low distant rail hum, quiet under speech. The title music is a slow, sparse loop of upright bass and vibraphone.",
